course: dictionary
lesson: 219
title: Alien in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so the context tells you which meaning is right. Look at the words around it first. «SETI scientists listen with radio telescopes for signals from intelligent life, but no confirmed alien signal has ever been found.» The scientists are listening to the sky, so alien here means from another planet.
explain: Alien can also be an adjective, meaning strange and very different from what you know. «The city felt alien to her.» Nobody has landed. She just finds the city strange and unfamiliar. Check it with the swap test: "The city felt strange to her" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Sometimes «alien» is used to mean made-up or unfamiliar. «Made-up «alien words» like «zib» are read on purpose.» The words are not from any real language. Ask yourself what word would fit, then try it in the sentence.
fact: Alien can be a noun («an alien», «aliens») or an adjective («alien»).
fact: As a noun, alien means a creature from another planet, as in stories and films.
fact: As an adjective, alien means strange and very different from what you know.
fact: In science, an alien species is a plant or animal brought to a place where it does not naturally live.
fact: No confirmed alien signal has ever been found by scientists, so life from another planet is still only a question.
exercise: «SETI scientists listen with radio telescopes for signals from intelligent life, but no confirmed alien signal has ever been found.» What does alien mean here? | Strange and unfamiliar to a person | A kind of plant that grows in water | *From another planet | Very old and worn out
exercise: «The city felt alien to her.» What does alien mean here? | Friendly and warm | *Strange and very different from what she knows | Very loud and busy | Made of stone
exercise: Yasmin says an alien species is a creature from a film. What is an alien species, really? | A person who was born in another country | *A plant or animal brought to a place where it does not naturally live | A castle built on a hill | A word that nobody can read
test: «Reading made-up «alien words» such as «zib» proves a child is decoding the sounds, not guessing from memory.» What does alien mean in «alien words»? | Very difficult to pronounce | *Made-up, not a real word from memory | Written in very old letters | Found in outer space
test: Which sentence uses alien as an adjective meaning strange? | *«The noisy market felt alien to the new student.» | «The alien was green and had three eyes.» | «An alien landed in the field last night.» | «The scientists searched for alien life.»
exam: Ben reads, «The Great Pyramid was built about 4,500 years ago for the pharaoh Khufu, not by aliens.» What does the sentence tell you about aliens? | Aliens helped the pharaoh rule | Aliens built the pyramid | Aliens built the pyramid long ago and then left | *Aliens did not build the pyramid; paid workers and farmers did
